IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpfta-unfair-practices`

-- Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003, ss 2 to 7, 12, 35, 36, 39, 40, First and Second Schedules -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_consumer-protection-fair-trading-act-2003_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

§ `s 2 -- consumer and supplier`

`an individual buying a phone for herself` MEANS `My position` WITH
    `I am an individual` IS TRUE
    `I acted exclusively in the course of business` IS FALSE
    `I held myself out as acting exclusively in the course of business` IS FALSE
    `I receive or have the right to receive the goods or services` IS TRUE
    `I must pay for goods or services supplied to another individual` IS FALSE

`a parent paying a tuition centre for a child` MEANS `My position` WITH
    `I am an individual` IS TRUE
    `I acted exclusively in the course of business` IS FALSE
    `I held myself out as acting exclusively in the course of business` IS FALSE
    `I receive or have the right to receive the goods or services` IS FALSE
    `I must pay for goods or services supplied to another individual` IS TRUE

`a sole trader who said he was buying only for his business` MEANS `My position` WITH
    `I am an individual` IS TRUE
    `I acted exclusively in the course of business` IS FALSE
    `I held myself out as acting exclusively in the course of business` IS TRUE
    `I receive or have the right to receive the goods or services` IS TRUE
    `I must pay for goods or services supplied to another individual` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `Am I a consumer` `an individual buying a phone for herself`
#ASSERT `Am I a consumer` `a parent paying a tuition centre for a child`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a consumer` `a sole trader who said he was buying only for his business`

`a phone shop` MEANS `The other side` WITH
    `it acted in the course of its business` IS TRUE
    `it provides goods or services to consumers` IS TRUE
    `it manufactures or assembles or produces goods` IS FALSE
    `it promotes the use or purchase of goods or services` IS FALSE
    `it is paid as a result of goods or services provided to consumers` IS FALSE
    `it is an employee or agent of a supplier` IS FALSE

`a neighbour selling her old sofa` MEANS `The other side` WITH
    `it acted in the course of its business` IS FALSE
    `it provides goods or services to consumers` IS TRUE
    `it manufactures or assembles or produces goods` IS FALSE
    `it promotes the use or purchase of goods or services` IS FALSE
    `it is paid as a result of goods or services provided to consumers` IS FALSE
    `it is an employee or agent of a supplier` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `Is the other side a supplier` `a phone shop`
#ASSERT NOT `Is the other side a supplier` `a neighbour selling her old sofa`

§ `s 2 and First Schedule -- consumer transaction`

`buying a phone` MEANS `My dealing` WITH
    `it is a supply or agreement to supply goods or services to me` IS TRUE
    `it is the acquisition of an estate or interest in immovable property` IS FALSE
    `it is a lease of residential property granted for rent` IS FALSE
    `it is a time share contract` IS FALSE
    `it is service under a contract of employment` IS FALSE

`buying a flat from a developer` MEANS `My dealing` WITH
    `it is a supply or agreement to supply goods or services to me` IS TRUE
    `it is the acquisition of an estate or interest in immovable property` IS TRUE
    `it is a lease of residential property granted for rent` IS FALSE
    `it is a time share contract` IS FALSE
    `it is service under a contract of employment` IS FALSE

`renting a flat` MEANS `My dealing` WITH
    `it is a supply or agreement to supply goods or services to me` IS TRUE
    `it is the acquisition of an estate or interest in immovable property` IS TRUE
    `it is a lease of residential property granted for rent` IS TRUE
    `it is a time share contract` IS FALSE
    `it is service under a contract of employment` IS FALSE

`work under my employment contract` MEANS `My dealing` WITH
    `it is a supply or agreement to supply goods or services to me` IS TRUE
    `it is the acquisition of an estate or interest in immovable property` IS FALSE
    `it is a lease of residential property granted for rent` IS FALSE
    `it is a time share contract` IS FALSE
    `it is service under a contract of employment` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `Is my dealing a consumer transaction` `buying a phone`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my dealing a consumer transaction` `buying a flat from a developer`
#ASSERT `Is my dealing a consumer transaction` `renting a flat`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my dealing a consumer transaction` `work under my employment contract`

§ `s 3 -- reach of Part 2`

#ASSERT `Does Part 2 reach my dealing` FALSE FALSE TRUE

§ `s 4 and Second Schedule -- unfair practice`

`a salesman's misleading answer` MEANS `What the supplier did` WITH
    `I might reasonably have been deceived or misled by it` IS TRUE
    `the supplier made a false claim` IS FALSE
    `the supplier took advantage of me` IS FALSE
    `the supplier knew or ought to have known I could not protect my own interests` IS FALSE
    `the supplier knew or ought to have known I could not understand the transaction` IS FALSE
    `it is another practice listed in the Second Schedule` IS FALSE
    `the price charged was substantially higher than the estimate given to me` IS FALSE
