§ `s 6 -- the money limit`

`a $35,000 claim less $6,000 set-off I admit` MEANS `My claim` WITH
    `I claim money` IS TRUE
    `the amount I claim` IS 35000
    `the set-off I admit in my particulars` IS 6000
    `I abandon the excess over the limit` IS FALSE
    `the value of the subject matter` IS 0

`a $35,000 claim` MEANS `My claim` WITH
    `I claim money` IS TRUE
    `the amount I claim` IS 35000
    `the set-off I admit in my particulars` IS 0
    `I abandon the excess over the limit` IS FALSE
    `the value of the subject matter` IS 0

`a $35,000 claim with the excess abandoned` MEANS `My claim` WITH
    `I claim money` IS TRUE
    `the amount I claim` IS 35000
    `the set-off I admit in my particulars` IS 0
    `I abandon the excess over the limit` IS TRUE
    `the value of the subject matter` IS 0

`a claim to have a $40,000 car delivered` MEANS `My claim` WITH
    `I claim money` IS FALSE
    `the amount I claim` IS 0
    `the set-off I admit in my particulars` IS 0
    `I abandon the excess over the limit` IS FALSE
    `the value of the subject matter` IS 40000

#ASSERT `Is my claim within the prescribed limit` `a $35,000 claim less $6,000 set-off I admit`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim within the prescribed limit` `a $35,000 claim`
#ASSERT `Is my claim within the prescribed limit` `a $35,000 claim with the excess abandoned`
#ASSERT NOT `Is my claim within the prescribed limit` `a claim to have a $40,000 car delivered`

#ASSERT `What is the most I can recover in my action` `a $35,000 claim with the excess abandoned` EQUALS JUST 30000
#ASSERT `What is the most I can recover in my action` `a $35,000 claim` EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `What is my home worth for the limit` (JUST 24000) (JUST 18000) NOTHING 900000 EQUALS JUST 18000
#ASSERT `What is my home worth for the limit` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING 800000 EQUALS JUST 80000
#ASSERT `What is my home worth for the limit` NOTHING NOTHING (JUST 2000) 800000 EQUALS NOTHING

